@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Philosophy
+
+For whoever proposes another service for larder. Start with the operating limits below: after the session-store and
+job-queue debates, [issue 70](../notes/issue-70.md) reopened the same argument over Elasticsearch for pantry item
+search, and volunteers asked to stop rediscovering it.
+
+## Tenets
+
+### Prefer what Postgres can do; add a service to operate only when Postgres cannot meet the need and two volunteers can restore it.
+
+Rules out adding a service just because someone can set it up: the proposal must establish what Postgres cannot do
+and which two volunteers can restore the new service when one is away. This limits what volunteers operate;
+the [external card gateway](architecture.md#parts) and a hosted service nobody on the team has to run are allowed.
+
+Applied in [keeping sessions in the database](adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md) and
+[running background jobs on Postgres](adrs/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md). The search proposal supplied
+another test: searching for "rice" took four seconds and missed "Rice, brown"; Postgres full-text search on the item
+name brought it to 40 ms and found the item, so the proposer chose that over Elasticsearch.
